## Convert the local.wast to wasm and json with wast2json
wast2json: https://github.com/WebAssembly/wabt/blob/main/docs/wast2json.md

```shell
$ wast2json chapter08.wast -o chapter08.json
```

```shell
$ wasm-objdump -d -x chapter08.0.wasm
```

## Debug with aarch64-linux
```shell
$ aarch64-linux-gnu-g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -O0 -g chapter08_main.cpp -o loop
$ qemu-aarch64 -L /usr/aarch64-linux-gnu ./loop

$ qemu-aarch64 -g 2345 -L /usr/aarch64-linux-gnu ./loop
vscode debug(F5)
```

### Build and test from the repository root
```shell
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
$ cmake --build build --target loop
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -R chapter08_arm64_gtest
```

## Tips
In ARM64 (AArch64) assembly, le_u is not a native instruction, so you express an "unsigned less than or equal to" comparison using the ls (Lower or Same) condition code alongside instructions like cmp, b.ls, or cset.
(Note: le_u is a standard numeric instruction in WebAssembly and intermediate representations like Cranelift/LLVM IR, which compilers lower to ARM64's ls condition).
See https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/WebAssembly/Reference/Numeric/le_u

Materialize a Boolean (cset): Sets a register to 1 if X0 <= X1, or 0 otherwise (matching WebAssembly's i64.le_u behavior).
```
armasm
cmp  x0, x1       // Compare X0 and X1
cset x2, ls       // X2 = 1 if X0 <= X1 (unsigned), else 0
```


